393	268,1750,760,2153 - 705,1738,765,1766	393. Piece of Madder, in flower.	A piece of Madder stem with a whorl of broad pointed leaves round it and a small cluster of star-shaped flowers springing from the axil above.
394	482,1291,759,1555	394. Half of a flower, magnified.	Half of a Madder flower magnified: the spreading pointed corolla-lobes with stamens between them, the two styles, and the ovary below cut to show its two cells.
395	523,1560,749,1741	395. Young fruits.	A short stalk bearing two young fruits, one large and round, the other small, with a narrow leaf beside them.
396	314,1565,471,1715	396. Ripe fruit.	The ripe fruit, a double berry of two rounded halves pressed together on a short stalk.
397	795,1314,1143,2161 - 1098,1690,1143,1885 - 1125,1300,1143,1630	397. Common Bluets.	A small tufted Bluets plant: a rosette of little leaves and fibrous roots at the base, and slender stalks bearing four-lobed, star-shaped flowers and buds.
398	1100,1691,1458,2155 - 1100,1885,1142,2155	398. Section of a flower lengthwise, magnified, and the corolla laid open.	A Bluets flower cut lengthwise and magnified: the tubular corolla opened with four stamens inside, the style running down to the two-celled ovary below.
399	1129,1299,1488,1626	399. Corolla of another flower laid open, and the style.	A second corolla slit and spread open, its four lobes turned back, the stamens set low in the tube and the long style standing in the middle.
